	THE ALGOL BINDER WAS WRITTEN TO ALLOW PROCEDURES TO BE SPECIFIED
IN A PROGRAM AT COMPILE TIME BUT ACTUALLY DECLARED OUTSIDE OF THE PROGRAM
(IN ANOTHER FILE FOR EXAMPLE). ALL IDENTIFIERS TO BE GLOBAL TO THE
SEPARATELY COMPILED PROCEDURE MUST BE DECLARED EXTERNAL IN BOTH THE MAIN
PROGRAM AND IN THE SEPARATELY COMPILED PROCEDURE.
	EXTERNAL DECLARATIONS ARE DECLARATIONS PRECEDDED BY THE WORD
EXTERNAL. PROCEDURES WHOSE BODY WILL BE SUPPLIED LATER (AT BIND TIME)
ARE DECLARED SIMILARLY TO FORWARD PROCEDURES WITH THE WORD 'EXTERNAL'
IN PLACE OF THE WORD 'FORWARD'.
	THE FORMAT OF A SEPARETLY COMPILED PROCEDURE IS:

	<SEP-PROC>::=<PROC HEAD><PROC BODY><END-THING>
	<END-THING>::= ; ! .

	IN OTHER WORDS, A SEPARATELY COMPILED PROCEDURE CONSISTS
OF EXACTLY THE PROCEDURE DECLARATION AND IS FOLLOWED BY EITHER A
PERIOD (.) OR A SEMI-COLON (;). EITHER IS ACCEPTED.

	AN EXAMPLE IS INCLUDED BELOW TO CLEARIFY MATTERS.

	THE INPUT COMMAND STRING TO THE BINDER IS AS FOLLOWS:

#[OUTCODE][,MAPFILE]=IN1[,IN2][,IN3]...[/OPTION1][/OPTION2]..

	THE DEFAULT EXTENSION OF THE OUTCODE FILE IS '.BND'
	THE DEFAULT EXTENSION OF THE MAP FILE IS '.MAP'
	    THIS FILE CONTAINS ALL RELOCATION INFORMATION.
	    IF THE FILE IS NOT SPECIFIED, THEN THE RELOCATION
	    INFORMATION IS PRINTED ON THE TERMINAL.
	THE DEFAULT EXTENSION ON EACH OF THE INPUT FILES IS '.ALG'.
	AS MANY INPUT FILES AS WILL FIT ON A LINE (72 COLS) WILL BE
	    ACCEPTED.

	THE OPTIONS ARE:
	    /C	CONTINUE INPUT ON NEXT LINE AFTER PROCESSING REST OF
		THIS LINE.
	    /G	BIND AND GO.

	IF THE /C OPTION IS SPECIFIED, A '*' WILL BE PRINTED ON THE NEXT
	LINE AND MORE INPUT FILES (AND OPTIONS) WILL BE ACCEPTED.

AS AN EXAMPLE:

.R ALGOL<CR>
 ----------
ALGOL INTERPETER V06.6.001
CODE FILE: <CR>
           ----
ALGOL V06.6.016
#TEST1[10],TEST1[5]=TEST1/L<CR>
 ------------------------------
(BLANK LINE)
CODE FILE: <CR>
	   ----
ALGOL V06.6.016
#TEST2[10],TEST2[5]=TEST2/L<CR>
 ------------------------------
(ANOTHER BLANK LINE)
CODE FILE: BINDER<CR>
	   ----------
BINDER V06.6.002
#TEST1=TEST1,TEST2/G<CR>
 -----------------------
(THE FOLLOWING IS RELOCATION INFORMATION PRINTED BY THE BINDER.)
.MD02		CHANGED FROM 000104 - X  TO  000112 - P
B.0000		CHANGED FROM 000105 - X  TO  000113 - P
(THE ABOVE 2 LINES ARE THE NEW ADDRESSES IN THE NEW PRT)
(BLANK LINE)
 B.0000(002) CHANGED TO SEGMENT 003
   DATA(003) CHANGED TO SEGMENT 004
  PRINT(001) CHANGED TO SEGMENT 005
(THE ABOVE 3 LINES ARE USEFUL IN CASE OF RUN TIME ERRORS. THEY ARE
	THE NEW SEGMENT NUMBERS OF THE PROGRAM AND DATA SEGMENTS
	OF THE FILE TEST2.ALG)
(THE NEXT 2 LINES ARE PRINTED BY THE PROGRAM)
THIS IS A TEST.
WHAT A TEST THIS IS.
(BLANK LINE)
CODE FILE: ^Z
	   --
.
